WEBVTT

00:00:00.285 --> 00:00:01.769
You add a receipt endpoint.

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:03.492
The replay gate is green.

00:00:03.663 --> 00:00:07.296
Before you ship, check whether the
recording ever asks for a receipt.

00:00:07.852 --> 00:00:13.553
The original mock-lab recording exercised
the Orders API, and the old gate exited

00:00:13.553 --> 00:00:15.665
zero after we added the route.

00:00:15.835 --> 00:00:19.415
Searching the recording for /receipt found
zero matches.

00:00:19.985 --> 00:00:22.063
Keep the first recording and baseline.

00:00:22.234 --> 00:00:26.509
Record the original traffic again, plus the
three calls in the receipt script.

00:00:26.679 --> 00:00:28.641
A valid order returns a receipt.

00:00:28.812 --> 00:00:32.943
An unknown order and a malformed ID each
return 404.

00:00:33.485 --> 00:00:36.780
Create a fresh baseline from the correct
implementation.

00:00:36.951 --> 00:00:39.524
This receipt has two lines and three items.

00:00:39.695 --> 00:00:44.055
Save the baseline that says three, then
confirm the updated gate passes.

00:00:44.619 --> 00:00:47.279
Temporarily change the handler to count
lines.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:50.277
The gate exits three and names the items
field.

00:00:50.448 --> 00:00:52.540
The response still has status 200.

00:00:52.711 --> 00:00:56.710
Restore the quantity sum, then verify the
gate exits zero again.

00:00:57.252 --> 00:00:59.506
Use the same pattern whenever you add a

00:00:59.506 --> 00:01:02.164
route to a service with an existing
recording.
